# Append to the VPS Caddyfile (the same Caddy that fronts waitdead-crm + waitdead-v2).
# Caddy auto-provisions TLS. Pick the real subdomain and point its DNS A record
# at the VPS IP first.
#
# ===========================================================================
# Philippines geo-block — STOPGAP ONLY. Read ops/vps/Caddyfile.snippet notes
# below and docs/PAYMENTS-SOTA-2026.md "Geo-block is a stopgap" before relying
# on this. The REAL access control is wallet-payment gating in the backend;
# geo-blocking is trivially bypassed with any VPN/proxy and only deters casual
# unpaid PH traffic while the payment cutover lands.
# ===========================================================================
#
# Pick ONE of the two approaches below depending on how this Caddy is fronted.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Approach A — MaxMind GeoIP2 module (Caddy reads the client IP -> country).
# Use when Caddy faces the public internet directly (our Contabo setup: Caddy
# is the edge, no Cloudflare in front). Requires a Caddy binary BUILT WITH the
# geoip2 module — stock Caddy does NOT include it:
#
#   xcaddy build --with github.com/zhangjiayin/caddy-geoip2
#
# and a MaxMind GeoLite2-Country.mmdb (free MaxMind account -> license key ->
# `geoipupdate`, or download the .mmdb). Point geoip2 at it in the GLOBAL
# options block at the TOP of the Caddyfile (NOT inside a site block):
#
#   {
#       geoip2_api maxmind {
#           account_id     YOUR_MAXMIND_ACCOUNT_ID
#           api_key        YOUR_MAXMIND_LICENSE_KEY
#           db_directory   /etc/caddy/geoip
#           update_url     "https://updates.maxmind.com"
#           update_frequency 86400
#       }
#   }
#
# Then inside the site block the @ph matcher tests the resolved country:
#
#   axie.waitdead.com {
#       encode zstd gzip
#       geoip2_vars strict          # populates {geoip2.country_code} from client IP
#       @ph expression `{geoip2.country_code} == "PH"`
#       respond @ph "Service not available in your region." 403
#       reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4010
#   }

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Approach B — Cloudflare CF-IPCountry header (NO custom Caddy build needed).
# Use ONLY if axie.waitdead.com is proxied THROUGH Cloudflare (orange cloud).
# Cloudflare injects a trusted `CF-IPCountry` header with the 2-letter country.
# This needs zero MaxMind setup and works on stock Caddy. SECURITY NOTE: trust
# this header ONLY when the request truly comes from Cloudflare — otherwise a
# client can forge CF-IPCountry. Restrict the upstream to Cloudflare IP ranges
# (trusted_proxies) or have the backend ignore the header unless remote_ip is CF.
#
#   axie.waitdead.com {
#       encode zstd gzip
#       @ph header CF-IPCountry PH
#       respond @ph "Service not available in your region." 403
#       reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4010
#   }

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default (NO geo-block) — what ships until one of the above is wired. The
# payment gate in the backend is the real control; uncomment a block above to
# add the PH stopgap on top.
axie.waitdead.com {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4010
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HONEST LIMITATION (do not oversell this to the owner):
#   * A VPN, proxy, Tor, or a relocated phone instantly bypasses a country
#     block — PH users who want in will be in. This is deterrence, not control.
#   * MaxMind GeoLite2 is ~accurate at the country level but mislabels some IPs;
#     expect a few false 403s (a non-PH user routed via a PH-registered IP).
#   * Mobile carriers and shared CGNAT can geolocate inconsistently.
#   * It blocks the WHOLE site (including the /api/payment/* flow), so a
#     legitimate PH user could never pay even if you wanted them to.
# The durable fix is the SOTA-2026 wallet-payment gate: a wallet only sees the
# tracker after an on-chain USDC payment (or an owner whitelist entry), which a
# VPN cannot fake. Treat the geo-block as a temporary lid while that lands, then
# consider removing it. See docs/PAYMENTS-SOTA-2026.md.
